#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1500.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069899} :activity/id #uuid "afe6da6e-0855-538d-ac54-1e34f990246c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050489} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069899 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186070016 :tutorial/content "We know how to integrate $\\cos{x}.$ But how do we integrate $\\cos{3x}?$ \n\nTo compute\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{3x} \\, \\textrm dx,\n$$\n\nwe can use substitution. If we let $u=3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = \\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** After solving an integral using substitution, we should always double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+C) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "075eaa34-761d-56ce-92f5-b498b52b92ac" :tutorial/math-academy-id 854 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "9a303692-65c8-5fbf-8f20-8a7e6213e724" :step/math-academy-id 617129 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069900}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069900 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068915 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068567 :question/id #uuid "0021ae6a-8ef8-564e-9c2e-fb5f9e8f7313" :question/math-academy-id "e-464" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle\\int 2 \\sin {\\left(\\dfrac x 3\\right)} \\,  \\textrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=\\dfrac x 3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac 1 3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x =3\\, \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "746d1bc6-98ec-59a1-bec6-9dcfb7081a5d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048332} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048777}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682522} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069047} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069149} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237798} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237799} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319064} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319362} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429932} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482716} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482718} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482722} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482724} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580891} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580915} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580918} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580944} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186601894} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676231} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676235} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676236} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676238} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676241} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676253} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676257} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676266} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676269} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676270} {:db/